# Generative AI Thermal Surrogate & Inverse Design

This repository contains a Scientific Machine Learning (SciML) sprint designed to build a state-of-the-art Generative AI Thermal Surrogate Model. The project demonstrates the progression from baseline deep learning to physics-constrained and resolution-invariant neural operators for 2D Conjugate Heat Transfer (CHT) simulations.

## 🚀 The 4-Week Roadmap

* [cite_start]**Week 1 (OpenFOAM Factory):** Automated generation of 2D Conjugate Heat Transfer simulations[cite: 1]. [cite_start]Extracted simulation data is mapped into PyTorch-ready tensors[cite: 2].
* [cite_start]**Week 2 (CNN Baseline):** Implementation of a standard Convolutional Neural Network to predict the thermal field[cite: 2]. [cite_start]Includes documentation of model failure when pushed Out-of-Distribution (OOD)[cite: 3].
* [cite_start]**Week 3 (PINN):** Deployment of a Physics-Informed Neural Network (PINN), embedding Navier-Stokes equations into the loss function to correct OOD hallucinations[cite: 3].
* [cite_start]**Week 4 (FNO):** Implementation of a Fourier Neural Operator (FNO) to prove resolution invariance across varying mesh densities[cite: 4].

## 📂 Repository Structure

Thermal_Surrogate/
├── data/                  # Immutable data assets
│   ├── raw/               # Raw extracted text/CSV from OpenFOAM
│   └── processed/         # Final PyTorch tensors (.pt files) ready for training
├── openfoam/              # The physics engine environment
│   ├── template/          # The golden, untouched reference case we built
│   └── runs/              # Automated run directories (run_001, run_002)
├── src/                   # Core Python package (Reusable logic)
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── data_parser.py     # Logic to extract OpenFOAM fields to NumPy
│   ├── dataset.py         # PyTorch Dataset and DataLoader classes
│   └── model.py           # PyTorch Neural Network architecture
├── scripts/               # Top-level execution (Automation)
│   ├── clone_case.sh      # Bash script to duplicate the template
│   └── run_sweep.py       # Python script to trigger Docker runs
├── models/                # Saved outputs
│   └── checkpoints/       # Saved model weights (.pth)
├── notebooks/             # Jupyter notebooks for EDA & visualization
├── .gitignore             # Tells git to ignore data/ and openfoam/runs/
├── requirements.txt       # Python dependencies
└── README.md              # The front page of your portfolio project

## 💻 Environment & Hardware

* [cite_start]**OS:** Ubuntu Linux 
* [cite_start]**Compute:** NVIDIA RTX 4070 (12GB VRAM) [cite: 16, 18]
